# UBSan reports inside OpenEXR that are its intended idiom, not faults.
# Used by Tools/fuzz.sh with the sanitized OpenEXR. Keep each entry narrow
# and say why it is benign.

# The frame-buffer convention: a slice's base pointer is the buffer minus the
# data window origin, which lands outside the allocation (and here wraps) for
# a negative window. Every EXR reader does this; the address is never
# dereferenced out of range. Found 2026-10-08, PXR24 tiled file, x = -256.
pointer-overflow:ImfInputFile.cpp
